TableCraft adaptation: deterministic normalized UTF-16 lookup records, a bounded Rust encoder, and a kana
vowel lookup, exported by docs/testing/ExportGeneralWeights.java and assembled by
docs/testing/build_general_weights.py. The Java implementation is not shipped as
an application dependency. These files are not Microsoft-published sort tables
or proof of native Microsoft Access compatibility.

The original derived like-legacy.fst and like-2010.fst sets retain the same
weight-data provenance and attribution. They encode complete raw single-unit
weight keys through TableCraft's current encoder, serialized with the MIT/
Unlicense fst 0.4.7 builder. They are regenerated by
scripts/regenerate_general_like.py and are not native Access index structures.
